  "claims": [
    "Within the retained pure Fin 31 presentation, a generic path can be moved past inverse eta using eta naturality and derived groupoid cancellation. No new generator is introduced.",
    "Forking two actual proof paths respects composition and higher comparisons, by the old tensor exchange calculus and contextual placement.",
    "For arbitrary opaque p:a->b and q:a->c, one actual tensorExpand step inside fork(p,q) reaches copy(a);fork(fst;p,snd;q). A separately specified restoration track returns to fork(p,q) using inverse eta and the two existing six-step projected tails.",
    "The restoration has exactly thirteen rewrite leaves. Expansion followed by restoration has fourteen equational leaves and is connected by an actual Four cell to the identity track. This is derived from eta naturality, splitting projected paths, the two new tensor/projection cells and the prior derived fork/eta triangle.",
    "The one-step expansion is compared to the inverse thirteen-step restoration by a derived Four cell. The restoration is not defined as the formal inverse of expansion and does not apply tensorExpand itself; p and q remain opaque payloads.",
    "For an atomic identity instance, the fourteen-leaf loop was not comparable to the identity in the previous PURE Fin 27 distribution presentation. The admissible tensorExpand-only annotation gives 1 versus 0 at the first output. No nonderivability in the richer mixed presentation is claimed.",
    "The existing MAC Fin 31 mixed presentation embeds the derived loop cancellation and expansion comparison with empty pure support. No new mixed basis or first-level rule is added.",
    "The expansion comparison is placed after one shared MAC.before computation and before fst discards one output copy. Its support is exactly singleton stage. Repaired joint-law equality in the updated checked model retains the correlated past, input and state."
  ],
